Subject: [PATCH 00894/11362] [outer-loop] Truncation inspected = BENIGN
 (post-answer rambling); fixed config; first valid on-policy

Operator-prompted inspection of truncated traces: only 8% are loops, 58% CONTAIN the gold
answer -- the model REACHES the answer ('The final answer is 30', gold=30) then rambles past
it without emitting <|im_end|>, hitting the cap. So truncation at 1024 is POST-answer
(last-number extraction still catches it) = largely benign, unlike v1's 256-tok PRE-answer
cutoff. No need for 8000. The repetition_penalty=1.3 bug was the real problem (fixed to 1.1,
temp 0.4): gen_trunc 0.80->0.14, own_correct 0.05->0.36. FIRST VALID on-policy result:
gold 0.667 (+0.43, STaR on own-correct works!) but verifier process_weighted 0.233 = base
(no lift, < unweighted 0.30) -> the verifier FAILS as a self-improvement reward (process!=
outcome in training); the gold ORACLE teaches. Bumped eval cap 768->1024 for clean 3-seed
confirm. Caveat: 1 seed, confirm pending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
